1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,980
Last time, the trolley was metal: strong.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,530
The fish tank was glass: transparent and waterproof.

3
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:08,610
Now: three water bottles!

4
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,100
Lock in first.

5
00:00:13,370 --> 00:00:15,780
A little squirrel is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:17,270
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:17,849 --> 00:00:19,179
Today you'll learn:

8
00:00:19,376 --> 00:00:21,646
One object, different materials.

9
00:00:21,847 --> 00:00:23,947
Many materials, one object.

10
00:00:24,151 --> 00:00:26,181
Choosing a suitable material.

11
00:00:27,863 --> 00:00:28,743
Round one.

12
00:00:29,043 --> 00:00:30,633
A water bottle for school.

13
00:00:30,913 --> 00:00:33,493
It must not break when dropped, and you want to see the

14
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:34,643
water inside.

15
00:00:34,923 --> 00:00:36,133
One, plastic.

16
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:37,413
Two, glass.

17
00:00:37,693 --> 00:00:38,683
Three, metal.

18
00:00:38,963 --> 00:00:40,443
Show me with your fingers.

19
00:00:46,914 --> 00:00:47,894
Locked in!

20
00:00:48,022 --> 00:00:48,742
Three!

21
00:00:49,032 --> 00:00:50,332
Metal is strong!

22
00:00:50,381 --> 00:00:50,991
One!

23
00:00:51,141 --> 00:00:53,211
I drop mine every PE lesson.

24
00:00:53,281 --> 00:00:54,481
Not one crack!

25
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:55,260
One.

26
00:00:56,338 --> 00:00:57,468
Look closer.

27
00:00:58,088 --> 00:01:00,058
Three bottles, full of water.

28
00:01:00,368 --> 00:01:01,458
No drips.

29
00:01:02,018 --> 00:01:05,048
Plastic, glass and metal are all waterproof.

30
00:01:06,057 --> 00:01:07,447
Can we see the water?

31
00:01:08,047 --> 00:01:09,307
Plastic, yes.

32
00:01:09,887 --> 00:01:11,007
Glass, yes.

33
00:01:11,597 --> 00:01:12,677
Metal, no.

34
00:01:13,387 --> 00:01:14,567
Now, a drop.

35
00:01:15,147 --> 00:01:17,047
The plastic bottle bounces.

36
00:01:17,637 --> 00:01:18,687
No break!

37
00:01:19,197 --> 00:01:20,437
The glass bottle?

38
00:01:21,017 --> 00:01:22,627
We do not drop glass.

39
00:01:22,762 --> 00:01:25,462
Glass is not as strong as plastic or metal.

40
00:01:29,587 --> 00:01:30,887
The answer is one.

41
00:01:31,157 --> 00:01:32,077
Plastic!

42
00:01:32,367 --> 00:01:33,357
One finger?

43
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:34,877
One finger up!

44
00:01:34,923 --> 00:01:35,513
Oh!

45
00:01:35,773 --> 00:01:37,933
Strong, but I cannot see my water!

46
00:01:38,361 --> 00:01:39,521
Say it with me!

47
00:01:40,227 --> 00:01:42,817
An object can be made from different materials.

48
00:01:43,387 --> 00:01:46,747
The choice of materials depends on the use of the object.

49
00:01:51,621 --> 00:01:52,891
Now look closer.

50
00:01:53,191 --> 00:01:54,311
A parked car.

51
00:01:54,966 --> 00:01:56,526
The tyres: rubber.

52
00:01:57,136 --> 00:01:58,646
They carry the whole car.

53
00:01:59,276 --> 00:02:00,546
Rubber is strong.

54
00:02:01,158 --> 00:02:02,788
The seats: fabric.

55
00:02:03,338 --> 00:02:04,768
Press, and they bend.

56
00:02:05,348 --> 00:02:06,908
Fabric is flexible.

57
00:02:07,521 --> 00:02:09,311
The windscreen: glass.

58
00:02:09,901 --> 00:02:13,371
Water cannot pass through, and we can see through it clearly.

59
00:02:13,996 --> 00:02:15,256
The body: metal.

60
00:02:15,276 --> 00:02:18,786
Strong, to protect the people inside.

61
00:02:20,192 --> 00:02:21,222
One car.

62
00:02:21,882 --> 00:02:23,082
Four parts.

63
00:02:23,682 --> 00:02:24,912
Four materials!

64
00:02:28,222 --> 00:02:29,522
Say it with me!

65
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,823
The materials are selected for the different functions of the parts based

66
00:02:33,843 --> 00:02:35,493
on their physical properties.

67
00:02:37,969 --> 00:02:39,799
Each part has its own job.

68
00:02:40,089 --> 00:02:42,329
So each part gets its own material.

69
00:02:42,676 --> 00:02:44,006
Be a drop of water!

70
00:02:44,356 --> 00:02:45,336
Shrink down.

71
00:02:45,606 --> 00:02:46,536
Quietly.

72
00:02:48,826 --> 00:02:52,196
You are a drop of water, falling from a watering can.

73
00:02:52,933 --> 00:02:53,883
Splash!

74
00:02:54,663 --> 00:02:56,153
You land on the glass.

75
00:02:56,933 --> 00:02:58,423
You cannot pass through.

76
00:02:59,088 --> 00:03:02,518
Through the glass, you see the fabric seats, dry inside.

77
00:03:03,255 --> 00:03:06,885
You roll over the metal, past the rubber tyre, to the ground.

78
00:03:09,589 --> 00:03:10,489
My notes!

79
00:03:10,619 --> 00:03:13,179
One: rubber tyres, because rubber is strong.

80
00:03:13,239 --> 00:03:16,809
Two: a glass windscreen, because glass is made from sand.

81
00:03:16,879 --> 00:03:19,829
Three: fabric seats, because fabric is flexible.

82
00:03:20,103 --> 00:03:21,003
Showdown!

83
00:03:21,313 --> 00:03:22,443
Double points.

84
00:03:22,713 --> 00:03:24,333
One line has a mistake.

85
00:03:24,623 --> 00:03:26,383
Line one, two, or three?

86
00:03:26,683 --> 00:03:28,153
Show me with your fingers.

87
00:03:34,628 --> 00:03:35,608
Locked in!

88
00:03:35,736 --> 00:03:36,366
Two!

89
00:03:36,516 --> 00:03:38,146
Sand is where glass comes from.

90
00:03:38,286 --> 00:03:39,676
It is not a property!

91
00:03:39,724 --> 00:03:40,514
Two.

92
00:03:40,764 --> 00:03:42,414
Glass is waterproof!

93
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:45,431
Two fingers?

94
00:03:45,671 --> 00:03:47,601
Put up two more on your score hand!

95
00:03:47,799 --> 00:03:49,059
Name the property.

96
00:03:49,339 --> 00:03:50,909
Then link it to the job.

97
00:03:52,343 --> 00:03:56,993
It is important to choose a material whose physical property is suitable

98
00:03:57,173 --> 00:03:59,613
for the intended use of the object.

99
00:04:01,088 --> 00:04:02,193
Say it with us!

100
00:04:02,853 --> 00:04:04,008
What is it for?

101
00:04:04,433 --> 00:04:05,414
The purpose!

102
00:04:09,253 --> 00:04:10,405
What can it do?

103
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:11,915
The property!

104
00:04:15,653 --> 00:04:16,693
So choose!

105
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:18,709
A suitable material!

106
00:04:22,808 --> 00:04:24,278
Show me your score hand!

107
00:04:24,558 --> 00:04:25,608
More than one?

108
00:04:25,908 --> 00:04:27,268
You beat the Buddies.

109
00:04:27,568 --> 00:04:28,628
Three fingers?

110
00:04:28,898 --> 00:04:29,908
High five!

111
00:04:30,413 --> 00:04:31,803
Did you spot the squirrel?

112
00:04:32,093 --> 00:04:33,933
It was on the tree by the cars!

113
00:04:34,203 --> 00:04:35,503
Tell someone at home.

114
00:04:36,291 --> 00:04:38,151
Next time: a school bag!

115
00:04:38,431 --> 00:04:41,121
Its strap must bend, and it must not tear.

116
00:04:41,401 --> 00:04:43,201
Which material would you choose?

117
00:04:43,471 --> 00:04:44,551
One, fabric.

118
00:04:44,831 --> 00:04:45,801
Two, metal.

119
00:04:46,071 --> 00:04:47,051
Three, wood.

120
00:04:47,331 --> 00:04:48,651
Lock in your answer!

121
00:04:48,699 --> 00:04:49,819
A metal strap!

122
00:04:49,919 --> 00:04:51,329
Nothing can tear that!

123
00:04:52,055 --> 00:04:54,255
Let's read today's key words together!

124
00:04:54,545 --> 00:04:55,305
Ready?

125
00:04:55,592 --> 00:04:56,402
Use.

126
00:04:57,626 --> 00:04:58,426
Parts.

127
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:00,530
Suitable.

128
00:05:01,881 --> 00:05:02,821
Well done!

129
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:04,904
Say it with us!

130
00:05:05,705 --> 00:05:06,455
Ready?

131
00:05:06,578 --> 00:05:07,238
One!

132
00:05:07,578 --> 00:05:08,278
two!

133
00:05:08,583 --> 00:05:09,758
Now you know!
